@startuml correction-dictionary-backend
' How the Levenshtein automaton is fed. The persistent vocab trie's Dictionary
' node handle (VocabTrieNodeRef = OverlayDictionaryNode) owns an Arc to each
' overlay node and re-resolves children on demand, so the automaton descends the
' FULL depth of the trie and runs directly over the mmap'd vocabulary — no in-RAM
' materialization. Green = the working, default path. Blue (dashed) = the optional
' materialized-trie side branch, reserved for small static dictionaries.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/correction-dictionary-backend.puml
' Source of truth for the dictionary-backend figure in docs/integration/lling-llang/dictionary-backend.md.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Dictionary backend — feeding the Levenshtein automaton

rectangle "**Google-Books checkpoint**\nPersistentVocabARTrie (mmap, ~13M terms)\nlock-free overlay, UTF-8" as pv #37474F

rectangle "**Dictionary::contains()**\nwalks the real trie — WORKS\n(used to skip in-vocabulary tokens)" as contains #2E7D32
rectangle "**Dictionary::root() / DictionaryNode::transition()**\nVocabTrieNodeRef = OverlayDictionaryNode<CharKey,u64>\nowns an Arc per overlay node → descends FULL depth" as trans #2E7D32

rectangle "**liblevenshtein Transducer**\nquery_with_distance(term, k)\nruns directly over the persistent trie" as auto #1565C0
rectangle "candidate corrections\n{the·1, ten·1, tea·2}" as cand #2E7D32

rectangle "**optional: DynamicDawgChar / DoubleArrayTrie**\nin-memory automaton materialized from\niter_terms() — small, static dictionaries only" as dawg #90A4AE

pv --> contains
pv --> trans
contains --> auto : membership test
trans --> auto : full traversal
auto --> cand

pv -[#607D8B,dashed]-> dawg : (only if small & static)
dawg -[#607D8B,dashed]-> auto : same generic\nDictionary interface

note bottom of trans
  Fixed in libdictenstein: VocabTrieNodeRef was superseded by the shared
  OverlayDictionaryNode, which holds the child Arc and re-resolves children
  on demand. The former depth-1 snapshot (childless nodes) is gone, so the
  generic LevenshteinCorrectionLayer runs **directly over the mmap'd
  SharedVocabARTrie** — no in-RAM copy, no libgrammstein change required.
end note
@enduml
